k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"kComponents()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/biconnectedComponents()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"biconnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BiconnectedComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity21BiconnectedComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/biconnectedcomponents()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The biconnected components, or blocks: the maximal biconnected subgraphs, as sets of edges,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which they partition (a self-loop is in no block). Blocks are ordered by their smallest edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, each listing its edges in ascending position. An isolated vertex, or one with only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loops, is in no block."}],"title":"biconnectedComponents()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/biconnectedComponents()","kind":